{
  "assessment": "The source reports trapped atom number versus lattice hold time for 3D and 1D optical lattices, with exponential-decay fits yielding lifetimes of 54 ms and 220 ms, respectively. The hold time is a common control, but the source does not provide a numeric domain for hold time beyond the exclusion of t_hold < 75 ms; no upper bound or full range is given. The initial atom number is not quantified in the text. Therefore, a complete numeric response with a finite common hold-time domain cannot be extracted, so case_authoring_ready is false.",
