    "citation": "Alan Bregazzi, Single-Beam Grating-Chip 3D and 1D Optical Lattices, Physical Review Letters (2025), DOI:10.1103/physrevlett.134.013001",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/physrevlett.134.013001",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2405.21065v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper demonstrates single-input-beam grating-chip optical lattices in 3D and 1D, reporting trapped atom number versus hold time with exponential-decay lifetimes, parametric resonance frequencies, and lattice properties. The selected cluster focuses on the lifetime measurements for 3D and 1D lattices.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "exponential_decay_fit",
      "statement": "The number of trapped atoms decays exponentially with hold time, with fitted lifetimes for the 3D and 1D lattices.",
